# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Double-blind review
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is mirrored by anonymous.4open.science, so anything
# committed here is visible to referees.
#
# CONVENTION: the tracked path CP_PromisingZone_SSR_TypeIError.qmd carries
# the ANONYMIZED content. The local working copy at that same path is the
# with-author source, so the file reads as permanently "modified" in
# `git status`. That is expected and must stay that way until acceptance.
#
# WARNING: `git add CP_PromisingZone_SSR_TypeIError.qmd` (or `git add -A`,
# or `git commit -a`) stages the with-author copy and deanonymizes the
# repository. .gitignore cannot prevent this, because the path is tracked.
# To update the committed manuscript, regenerate the anonymized copy and
# stage it without touching the working tree:
#
#     Rscript R/make_anon.R
#     git update-index --cacheinfo 100644,\
#       $(git hash-object -w CP_PromisingZone_SSR_TypeIError_anon.qmd),\
#       CP_PromisingZone_SSR_TypeIError.qmd
#
# After acceptance, commit the with-author source directly and delete this
# block along with the two entries below.

# Generated anonymized copy: an intermediate, staged into the path above
# rather than committed under its own name.
CP_PromisingZone_SSR_TypeIError_anon.qmd

# The anonymization script itself names the authors, the organisation and
# the real repository URL in its FORBIDDEN list, so it cannot ship while
# review is blind. Commit it after acceptance.
R/make_anon.R

